    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0475" n="467" xml:id="pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.733/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-22T14:00:00-04:00">July 22, 1939—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>309. Your 681, July 20, 9 p.m. I have nothing to add to the instructions which we
                    have already sent you concerning our Consulate General at Prague.<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d419-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d419-f1" n="10" xml:id="d419-f1-content">
                <p>No further action was taken on the part of the United States; the Consulate
                    General at Prague continued to function without interference until the German
                    Foreign Office in September 1940 requested that the Consulate be closed. The
                    Consulate was officially closed October 15, 1940.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
